request.description:
Liveness probe. No API key needed (nor on `/api/config` and `/openapi.json`) — the collection still sends the bearer token, which is ignored here. Returns `{"status": "ok"}`. This is what the compose healthcheck curls over loopback, which keeps working with the egress firewall on (loopback is ACCEPTed by its first iptables rule). See OPEN_TERMINAL.md § Verifying the connection.

#### Schemas

No authentication (no API key dependency).

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["status"],
  "properties": {
    "status": {"const": "ok"}
  }
}
```

FastAPI's generated OpenAPI document. This is the contract Open WebUI consumes: `utils/tools.py::set_terminal_servers` fetches `<url><path>` ONCE at startup (path defaults to `/openapi.json`) and turns every operation with `include_in_schema=True` into a native function-calling tool on the model. Endpoints marked `include_in_schema=False` in the source (health, api/config, system, cwd, view, serve, mkdir, move, delete, upload, archive, compare, skills, ports, the port proxy, and the PTY session routes — `/api/terminals/user/*` excepted) are reachable over HTTP but are UI/client surface, not model tools. No API key needed: FastAPI serves this document without the routes' key check.

A failure or timeout here is what produces the chat-side 503 “Terminal unavailable” — re-saving the connection in Admin Settings → Integrations → Open Terminal re-runs the fetch.

#### Schemas

No authentication (FastAPI serves it without the routes' API-key dependency). Lists only the routes without `include_in_schema=False` -- on the box 16 paths: `/info`, the file read / write / search tools, `/execute*` and `/api/terminals/user/*` -- which Open WebUI turns into the model's tools.

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "$comment": "OpenAPI 3.1 document",
  "required": ["openapi", "info", "paths"],
  "properties": {
    "openapi": {"type": "string", "description": "`3.1.0`"},
    "info": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "required": ["title", "version"],
      "properties": {
        "title": {"const": "Open Terminal"},
        "version": {"type": "string"}
      }
    },
    "paths": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": true},
    "components": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": true}
  }
}
```

Feature-flag discovery for clients: `{"features": {"terminal": bool, "notebooks": bool, "system": bool}}`, driven by OPEN_TERMINAL_ENABLE_TERMINAL / _ENABLE_NOTEBOOKS / _ENABLE_SYSTEM_PROMPT. Open WebUI's connection **Verify** button falls back to this endpoint to tell a plain Open Terminal apart from the Enterprise “Terminals” orchestrator. Not in the OpenAPI schema. No API key needed.

#### Schemas

No authentication (no API key dependency).

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["features"],
  "properties": {
    "features": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "required": ["terminal", "notebooks", "system"],
      "properties": {
        "terminal": {"type": "boolean", "description": "OPEN_TERMINAL_ENABLE_TERMINAL"},
        "notebooks": {"type": "boolean", "description": "OPEN_TERMINAL_ENABLE_NOTEBOOKS"},
        "system": {"type": "boolean", "description": "OPEN_TERMINAL_ENABLE_SYSTEM_PROMPT"}
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Returns `{"prompt": "..."}` — the generated system prompt describing the environment (OS, kernel, architecture, host, user, shell and Python version) with OPEN_TERMINAL_INFO appended — or the OPEN_TERMINAL_SYSTEM_PROMPT template, when that is set. Open WebUI fetches this at startup and injects it for any model with the terminal attached, so it is the cheapest way to see exactly what the model is told about this box.

Disabled (404) when OPEN_TERMINAL_ENABLE_SYSTEM_PROMPT=false. Errors: 401 on a bad key.

#### Schemas

Mounted only with OPEN_TERMINAL_ENABLE_SYSTEM_PROMPT (else 404).

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["prompt"],
  "properties": {
    "prompt": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "OS, kernel, architecture, host, user, shell and Python version, then OPEN_TERMINAL_INFO; or OPEN_TERMINAL_SYSTEM_PROMPT with its `{{...}}` variables filled"
    }
  }
}
```

Returns `{"info": "<OPEN_TERMINAL_INFO>"}` — the operator context string verbatim. **The route only exists when OPEN_TERMINAL_INFO is non-empty**; with it blank you get a 404, not an empty string. Unlike most of the discovery endpoints this one IS in the OpenAPI schema, so it also reaches the model as a `get_info` tool. Set in the `## Open Terminal subsystem` block of .env. Errors: 401 on a bad key.

#### Schemas

Mounted only when OPEN_TERMINAL_INFO is non-empty (else 404). The model's `get_info` tool.

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["info"],
  "properties": {
    "info": {"type": "string", "description": "OPEN_TERMINAL_INFO, verbatim"}
  }
}
```

TCP ports currently listening inside the container, as `{"ports": [...]}`. In multi-user mode only ports owned by X-User-Id's Linux account are listed; in single-user mode only those owned by descendants of the server process. Backs the “a dev server is running” affordance in the UI.

Note the container publishes no host port and sits alone with openwebui on terminal_net, so anything listening here is reachable only from openwebui. Not in the OpenAPI schema. Errors: 401 on a bad key.

#### Schemas

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["ports"],
  "properties": {
    "ports": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "TCP ports listening in the container that the caller owns: X-User-Id's account in multi-user mode, else the server's descendant processes",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "required": ["port", "pid", "process"],
        "properties": {
          "port": {"type": "integer"},
          "pid": {"type": ["integer", "null"]},
          "process": {"type": ["string", "null"], "description": "The process name"}
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Current working directory for this X-Session-Id, plus `home`, plus an optional `root` object describing the file browser's visual root (driven by OPEN_TERMINAL_FILE_BROWSER_ROOT — `home` by default, an explicit path, `{{home}}/project`, or `filesystem` to opt out).

`root` is a UI hint only: it hides parent navigation above a friendly starting point and does NOT restrict commands or the file APIs. Session cwds expire after OPEN_TERMINAL_SESSION_CWD_TTL (7 days, sliding). Not in the OpenAPI schema. Errors: 401.

#### Schemas

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["cwd", "home"],
  "properties": {
    "cwd": {"type": "string", "description": "X-Session-Id's working directory, else the home"},
    "home": {"type": "string"},
    "root": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "description": "The file browser's visual root (OPEN_TERMINAL_FILE_BROWSER_ROOT); absent for `filesystem`. A UI hint, not a restriction",
      "required": ["path", "label"],
      "properties": {
        "path": {"type": "string"},
        "label": {"type": "string"}
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Remember a working directory for this X-Session-Id; subsequent relative paths in /files/* and /execute resolve against it. Returns `{"cwd": "<resolved>"}`. Body is the same one-field shape as /files/mkdir.

Errors: 404 when the directory does not exist (single-user mode only — in multi-user mode the check is skipped because the stat would run as the wrong account), 401.

#### Schemas

404 when the directory does not exist (single-user mode only).

Request body (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "$comment": "MkdirRequest, reused: here the directory to remember",
  "required": ["path"],
  "properties": {
    "path": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Directory path to create. Parent directories are created automatically."
    }
  }
}
```

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["cwd"],
  "properties": {
    "cwd": {"type": "string", "description": "The resolved path"}
  }
}
```

Structured listing of a directory: `{"dir", "writable", "entries": [...]}`. Relative paths resolve against the session cwd when X-Session-Id is sent. Exposed to the model as the `list_files` tool. Errors: 404 when the directory does not exist, 401.

#### Schemas

The model's `list_files` tool. 404 when the directory does not exist.

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["dir", "writable", "entries"],
  "properties": {
    "dir": {"type": "string", "description": "The resolved directory"},
    "writable": {"type": "boolean"},
    "entries": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "$comment": "UserFS.listdir entry (open_terminal/utils/fs.py)",
        "required": ["name", "type", "size", "modified", "writable"],
        "properties": {
          "name": {"type": "string"},
          "type": {"enum": ["file", "directory"]},
          "size": {"type": "integer", "description": "Bytes (st_size)"},
          "modified": {"type": "number", "description": "Unix seconds (st_mtime)"},
          "writable": {"type": "boolean"}
        }
      },
      "description": "Sorted by name"
    }
  }
}
```

Ask the CLIENT to show a file to the user. Returns only `{"path", "exists"}` — it does not serve content. Open WebUI intercepts the tool result and opens its preview pane. Exposed as the `display_file` tool; models are told to use it when the user says “show me” rather than when the model itself needs to read the file. Errors: 401.

#### Schemas

The model's `display_file` tool: serves nothing; Open WebUI opens the file in its preview pane.

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["path", "exists"],
  "properties": {
    "path": {"type": "string"},
    "exists": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Whether it is a file"}
  }
}
```

Write TEXT content to a path, creating parent directories and overwriting any existing file. Returns `{"path", "size"}` where size is the UTF-8 byte length. There is no append mode and no binary mode — use /files/upload for bytes. Exposed as the `write_file` tool. Errors: 400 on an OS error (permissions, ENOSPC), 401.

#### Schemas

The model's `write_file` tool. 400 on an OS error.

Request body (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "path": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Absolute or relative path to write to. Parent directories are created automatically."
    },
    "content": {"type": "string", "description": "Text content to write to the file."}
  },
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["path", "content"],
  "additionalProperties": true
}
```

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["path", "size"],
  "properties": {
    "path": {"type": "string", "description": "The resolved absolute path"},
    "size": {"type": "integer", "description": "Bytes written"}
  }
}
```

Exact find-and-replace inside one file, applied sequentially. Each chunk takes `target` / `replacement` and may narrow the search with `start_line` / `end_line`, or opt into replacing every occurrence with `allow_multiple` (default false — an ambiguous match is an error, not a silent first-hit). This is the surgical-edit tool models should reach for instead of rewriting a file with /files/write. Exposed as `replace_file_content`. Errors: 404 file not found, 400 target not found or ambiguous, 401.

#### Schemas

The model's `replace_file_content` tool. 404 when the file is not there; 400 when a target is not found, or found more than once without `allow_multiple`.

Request body (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "path": {"type": "string", "description": "Path to the file to modify."},
    "replacements": {
      "items": {
        "properties": {
          "target": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Exact string to find. Must match precisely, including whitespace."
          },
          "replacement": {"type": "string", "description": "Content to replace the target with."},
          "start_line": {
            "anyOf": [
              {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1.0},
              {"type": "null"}
            ],
            "description": "Narrow the search to lines at or after this (1-indexed)."
          },
          "end_line": {
            "anyOf": [
              {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1.0},
              {"type": "null"}
            ],
            "description": "Narrow the search to lines at or before this (1-indexed)."
          },
          "allow_multiple": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "If true, replaces all occurrences. If false, errors when multiple matches are found.",
            "default": false
          }
        },
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["target", "replacement"],
        "additionalProperties": true
      },
      "type": "array",
      "description": "List of find-and-replace operations to apply sequentially."
    }
  },
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["path", "replacements"],
  "additionalProperties": true
}
```

Response `200` (`application/json`) — `size`: the new file's bytes:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["path", "size"],
  "properties": {
    "path": {"type": "string", "description": "The resolved absolute path"},
    "size": {"type": "integer", "description": "Bytes written"}
  }
}
```

body.raw:
{
  "path": "hello.py",
  "replacements": [
    {
      "target": "hello from open-terminal",
      "replacement": "hello from the Zeo terminal",
      "allow_multiple": false
    }
  ]
}

request.description:
Create a directory, parents included. Returns `{"path"}`. Idempotent for an existing directory. Not in the OpenAPI schema (models create directories with a shell command instead). Errors: 400 on an OS error, 401.

#### Schemas

400 on an OS error.

Request body (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "$comment": "MkdirRequest",
  "required": ["path"],
  "properties": {
    "path": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Directory path to create. Parent directories are created automatically."
    }
  }
}
```

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["path"],
  "properties": {
    "path": {"type": "string"}
  }
}
```

Move or rename a file or directory. Returns `{"source", "destination"}`. Deliberately non-destructive: it refuses rather than clobbering. Not in the OpenAPI schema. Errors: 404 source missing, 400 destination's parent directory missing, 409 destination already exists, 401.

#### Schemas

404 when the source is missing, 400 when the destination's parent is, 409 when the destination exists.

Request body (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "$comment": "MoveRequest",
  "required": ["source", "destination"],
  "properties": {
    "source": {"type": "string", "description": "Path to the file or directory to move."},
    "destination": {"type": "string", "description": "Destination path (new location)."}
  }
}
```

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["source", "destination"],
  "properties": {
    "source": {"type": "string"},
    "destination": {"type": "string"}
  }
}
```

Permanently delete a file or directory (recursively). Returns `{"path", "type"}` where type is `file` or `directory`. No trash, no undo — the `open_terminal_home` volume has no snapshotting. Not in the OpenAPI schema. Errors: 404 path not found, 400 on an OS error, 401.

#### Schemas

Recursive, no undo. 404 when the path is not there, 400 on an OS error.

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["path", "type"],
  "properties": {
    "path": {"type": "string"},
    "type": {"enum": ["file", "directory"]}
  }
}
```

Upload one file via multipart/form-data into `directory`, which is created if missing. The stored filename is the basename of the uploaded file; the `directory` query param controls the location. Returns `{"path", "size"}`.

This is what a chat-composer drag-and-drop hits when the connection has `config.chat_uploads: "filesystem"` — files land in the user's terminal home instead of Open WebUI's RAG store. In Postman, pick a local file in the `file` form field (the value is left blank on purpose). Errors: 403 permission denied, 400 on an OS error, 401.

#### Schemas

`directory` (a query parameter) is created when missing; the file keeps its own basename. 403 on a permission error, 400 on another OS error.

Request body (`multipart/form-data`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["file"],
  "properties": {
    "file": {
      "type": "string",
      "contentMediaType": "application/octet-stream",
      "description": "The file to upload."
    }
  }
}
```

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["path", "size"],
  "properties": {
    "path": {"type": "string", "description": "The resolved absolute path"},
    "size": {"type": "integer", "description": "Bytes written"}
  }
}
```

Bundle files and/or directories into a single ZIP and stream it back as `application/zip`. Directories are walked recursively. The download filename is derived from the input: the basename for a single path, `download.zip` for several. Backs the file browser's multi-select download. Not in the OpenAPI schema. Errors: 400 empty `paths`, 404 when any path is missing, 401.

#### Schemas

400 for an empty `paths`, 404 when any path is not there.

Request body (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "$comment": "ArchiveRequest",
  "required": ["paths"],
  "properties": {
    "paths": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {"type": "string"},
      "description": "List of file or directory paths to include in the ZIP archive."
    }
  }
}
```

Response `200` (`application/zip`) — `attachment; filename="<name>.zip"`: the basename of a single path, else `download.zip`.

Diff the text of two files for the UI's side-by-side view — documents (PDF, Office, …) through their text extractors — in a worker running as the caller's account, at most 60 s. The body is `CompareRequest` (`open_terminal/utils/file_compare.py`): `original` and `revised`, two file paths resolved against the session cwd, and optional `ignore_whitespace` (default false). Returns `{original, revised, additions, deletions, hunks}`. Not in the OpenAPI schema and not a model tool. Errors: 404 / 403 for a missing / forbidden file, 422 when its text cannot be extracted, 408 past 60 s, 401.

#### Schemas

A line diff of two files' text (documents through their text extractor), run as the caller's account in a 60 s worker. 404 / 403 for a missing / forbidden file, 422 when the text cannot be extracted, 408 past 60 s.

Request body (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "$comment": "CompareRequest (open_terminal/utils/file_compare.py)",
  "required": ["original", "revised"],
  "properties": {
    "original": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1, "description": "The first file's path"},
    "revised": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1, "description": "The second file's path"},
    "ignore_whitespace": {"type": "boolean", "default": false}
  }
}
```

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["original", "revised", "additions", "deletions", "hunks"],
  "properties": {
    "original": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "required": ["path", "name", "notices"],
      "properties": {
        "path": {"type": "string"},
        "name": {"type": "string"},
        "notices": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {"type": "string"},
          "description": "What the text extraction leaves out"
        }
      }
    },
    "revised": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "required": ["path", "name", "notices"],
      "properties": {
        "path": {"type": "string"},
        "name": {"type": "string"},
        "notices": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {"type": "string"},
          "description": "What the text extraction leaves out"
        }
      }
    },
    "additions": {"type": "integer"},
    "deletions": {"type": "integer"},
    "hunks": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "required": ["header", "lines"],
        "properties": {
          "header": {"type": "string", "description": "`@@ -a,b +c,d @@`"},
          "lines": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": true,
              "required": ["type", "oldNumber", "newNumber", "content", "segments"],
              "properties": {
                "type": {"enum": ["context", "removed", "added"]},
                "oldNumber": {"type": ["integer", "null"]},
                "newNumber": {"type": ["integer", "null"]},
                "content": {"type": "string"},
                "revisedContent": {"type": "string", "description": "On `context` lines only"},
                "segments": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "additionalProperties": true,
                    "required": ["text", "changed"],
                    "properties": {
                      "text": {"type": "string"},
                      "changed": {"type": "boolean"}
                    }
                  },
                  "description": "Word-level changes of a removed / added pair"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Search file CONTENTS across a directory tree. Returns structured matches with file path, line number, and the matching line; binary files are skipped. Set `match_per_line=false` to get just the list of matching filenames. Exposed as the `grep_search` tool. Errors: 404 search path not found, 400 invalid regex, 401.

#### Schemas

The model's `grep_search` tool. 404 when the path is not there, 400 for a bad regex.

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["query", "path", "matches", "truncated"],
  "properties": {
    "query": {"type": "string"},
    "path": {"type": "string"},
    "matches": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "required": ["file"],
        "properties": {
          "file": {"type": "string"},
          "line": {"type": "integer", "description": "With `match_per_line` (the default)"},
          "content": {"type": "string", "description": "The matching line, with `match_per_line`"}
        }
      }
    },
    "truncated": {"type": "boolean", "description": "`max_results` was reached"}
  }
}
```

Find files by glob PATTERN. Returns relative path, type, size, and mtime per hit. Use this when you know the shape of the name; use /files/search when you only know part of it. Exposed as the `glob_search` tool. Errors: 404 search directory not found, 401.

#### Schemas

The model's `glob_search` tool. 404 when the directory is not there.

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["pattern", "path", "matches", "truncated"],
  "properties": {
    "pattern": {"type": "string"},
    "path": {"type": "string"},
    "matches": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "required": ["path", "type", "size", "modified"],
        "properties": {
          "path": {"type": "string", "description": "Relative to `path`"},
          "type": {"enum": ["file", "directory"]},
          "size": {"type": "integer"},
          "modified": {"type": "number"}
        }
      }
    },
    "truncated": {"type": "boolean"}
  }
}
```

Fuzzy, RANKED search by filename — the file browser's quick-open box. Prefers git-tracked files where the directory is a repo. Exposed as the `search_files` tool. Errors: 404 search directory not found, 401.

#### Schemas

The model's `search_files` tool: ranked filename matches (git-tracked files when the directory is a repo). 404 when the directory is not there.

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["results"],
  "properties": {
    "results": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "required": ["path", "name", "type", "size", "modified"],
        "properties": {
          "path": {"type": "string"},
          "name": {"type": "string"},
          "type": {"enum": ["file", "directory"]},
          "size": {"type": "integer"},
          "modified": {"type": "number"}
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Ranked search by name, path AND content: each result says whether its name matched and carries up to three content matches (`line`, `column`, `text`); paged by `offset` / `limit` (at most 100), `next_offset` null on the last page. Parameters: `query` (literal text, required), `path`, `show_hidden`, `offset`, `limit`. In the OpenAPI schema, so exposed as the `match_files` tool. Errors: 400 blank query, 404 search directory not found, 401.

#### Schemas

The model's `match_files` tool: ranked name, path and content matches, paged by `offset` / `limit` (at most 100). 400 for a blank query, 404 when the directory is not there.

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["results", "next_offset"],
  "properties": {
    "results": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "required": ["path", "relative_path", "name", "type", "name_match", "content_matches"],
        "properties": {
          "path": {"type": "string"},
          "relative_path": {"type": "string"},
          "name": {"type": "string"},
          "type": {"enum": ["file", "directory"]},
          "name_match": {"type": "boolean"},
          "content_matches": {
            "type": "array",
            "description": "At most 3 per file",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": true,
              "required": ["line", "column", "text"],
              "properties": {
                "line": {"type": "integer"},
                "column": {"type": "integer"},
                "text": {"type": "string"}
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "next_offset": {"type": ["integer", "null"], "description": "null on the last page"}
  }
}
```

