Run a shell command. The command always starts in the BACKGROUND and is identified by the returned `id`; `wait` only controls how long the server blocks before answering. Supports chaining, pipes, and redirection. Response: `{id, command, status, exit_code, output, truncated, next_offset, log_path}`.

With `wait` omitted the server falls back to OPEN_TERMINAL_EXECUTE_TIMEOUT (empty in this deployment → return immediately), so the normal flow is: POST /execute → poll GET /execute/{id}/status with the previous `next_offset` until `status` is `done`. In multi-user mode the command runs as X-User-Id's Linux account via `sudo -u`.

Egress is allowlisted (OPEN_TERMINAL_ALLOWED_DOMAINS) — a curl to an unlisted host fails at DNS, not at connect. Exposed as the `run_command` tool. Errors: 401.

#### Schemas

The model's `run_command` tool. The command always runs in the background; `wait` (seconds, 0-300; OPEN_TERMINAL_EXECUTE_TIMEOUT when absent) only holds the answer.

Request body (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "command": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Shell command to execute. Supports chaining (&&, ||, ;), pipes (|), and redirections.",
      "examples": ["echo hello", "ls -la && whoami"]
    },
    "cwd": {
      "anyOf": [
        {"type": "string"},
        {"type": "null"}
      ],
      "description": "Working directory for the command. Defaults to the server's current directory if not set."
    },
    "env": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "additionalProperties": {"type": "string"},
          "type": "object"
        },
        {"type": "null"}
      ],
      "description": "Extra environment variables merged into the subprocess environment."
    }
  },
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["command"],
  "additionalProperties": true
}
```

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "$comment": "execute() / get_status() in open_terminal/main.py; output from open_terminal/utils/log.py read_log",
  "required": [
    "id",
    "command",
    "status",
    "exit_code",
    "output",
    "truncated",
    "next_offset",
    "log_path"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "id": {"type": "string", "description": "`YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-<6 hex>`"},
    "command": {"type": "string"},
    "status": {"enum": ["running", "done", "killed"]},
    "exit_code": {"type": ["integer", "null"], "description": "null while running"},
    "output": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "Output entries since `offset` (the last `tail` of them when `tail` is set)",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "required": ["type", "data"],
        "properties": {
          "type": {
            "enum": ["stdout", "stderr", "output"],
            "description": "`output` when the command runs on a PTY"
          },
          "data": {"type": "string"}
        }
      }
    },
    "truncated": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "Entries were skipped: rotated out of the log, or cut by `tail`"
    },
    "next_offset": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Pass back as `offset` to read only new output"
    },
    "log_path": {"type": ["string", "null"], "description": "The process's JSONL log file"}
  }
}
```

