Poll a command: status, exit code, and output SINCE `offset`. Reads are non-consuming — each reader keeps its own offset — so pass back the `next_offset` from the previous response to stream incrementally. `wait` blocks until the process exits or the timeout elapses, whichever comes first.

A finished process is forgotten 5 minutes after it ends: its status is then a 404 and it leaves GET /execute. A log past OPEN_TERMINAL_MAX_LOG_SIZE (50 MB) keeps only its newer half, and `truncated` tells a reader it missed output. Exposed as `get_process_status`. Errors: 404 unknown process (or one owned by a different user/session), 401.

